# Publish every verified task

This rule is permanent. It applies to every Thrones of Myth development task.

`main` is the only active development branch. Do not create a feature branch or an extra worktree for a routine task. Do not develop in a stale checkout. Fetch `origin/main` and confirm this workspace is that commit before starting.

After a task is implemented, tested, and recorded in the coverage register, finish it in this order:

1. Implement the functional change.
2. Run the tests in `scripts/publish-tests.json`, plus the regression tests for the system you changed. That plan covers only the systems it names. It is not a full game audit. Add the new test command to the plan before publishing.
3. Update the coverage register and the development report with the commands that actually ran.
4. Commit only the verified files. The message must say why the change exists. If the prompt changed no files, do not create an empty commit. If tests fail or the work is incomplete, keep the files, do not commit, and say that publication is blocked.
5. From the worktree where `main` is checked out, push with `python scripts/publish_task.py --push`. The script refuses any other branch, a dirty worktree, and a diverged remote. It does not switch branches, merge, reset, or overwrite uncommitted files.
6. Report the commit, the push, and the remote SHA only after `git rev-parse origin/main` matches the pushed commit. Never claim a push that was not confirmed. Never leave a completed commit unpushed.

Do not start the next feature while a completed feature is still unpushed. Write `.cursor/publish-pending` after the tests pass, and remove it only after `origin/main` confirms the commit. If that marker is still present at the end of a turn, the stop hook reminds you to publish before any new feature.

If a test fails, do not commit or push. If GitHub rejects the push, or `origin/main` is not a fast-forward ancestor of the commit, stop and report the blocker. Never force-push, never skip hooks, and never bypass branch protection.

Keep these untracked and out of every commit: the two original Excel research workbooks, credentials, `.env` files, kingdom saves, and SQLite databases. A machine-local hook path must not be committed.

Mana stays an ordinary resource. Aether stays premium. Do not change world schema 20 or health protocol 16 unless the task says so and a migration test exists. Do not build custom 3D assets unless the task asks for them. Do not call a paid OpenAI API. Do not start a paid review loop or generate automatic follow-up prompts. This rule is about Git publication on `main`.
